From 8cf7230cf1021351b2c63d3858b5c43bcc84a349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:40:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(app): stamp each mill-turn operation that the posed
 law can read

#3096 posts an unstamped rotary kind on a mill-turn in the mill order
(rotary_traverse::mill_post_rotary), which reads the path. The stamp
cannot read the path, so it now takes each mill and mill-turn setup as
the mill order: a word too many reads a cache Stale once; a word too few
would keep an unjudged cache fresh.

Refs #3084

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs b/crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs
index 4102074f2..8eed33538 100644
--- a/crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs
+++ b/crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs
@@ -89,10 +89,14 @@ pub(super) fn turn_of(params: &OpParams, mill: bool, rotaries: Option<&[AxisLimi
 /// #3084: whether the posed law reads this operation on its setup's
 /// machine (a refusal counts: the law reads it too). Its op stamp then
 /// takes one more word, so a cache judged without the law reads Stale
-/// once; no other stamp moves. A lathe tool is no milling tool, but the
-/// stamp does not know the tool: it reads a milling one, as #3083's does.
